__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
data/raw/.espn_cache_*.json
data/raw/.sleeper_cache.json
data/raw/.ffc_*.json
data/raw/.outcomes_*.json
adp_gap_report.md
adp_gap_report.csv
data/validation_report.html
data/backtest_report.html
data/backtest_results*.json
data/snapshots/*
# ...except the futures archive. The other snapshot sources are recoverable:
# FFC's historical ADP was probed and found FROZEN (a fresh 2015 fetch matches a
# months-old cache for all 201 players), and ESPN rankings are re-derivable.
# ESPN preserves NO historical award futures at all -- 2020-2024 return zero
# priced runners -- so these files are the only record that will ever exist, and
# leaving them on one machine's disk is a single point of failure for data that
# cannot be re-fetched. See docs/VEGAS_DATA_RESEARCH.md.
!data/snapshots/futures_*.json
